WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk about,
in all seriousness,

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
insofar as we
talk about politeness,

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
which will be
an interesting thing

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.140 line:92%
in this campaign going forward

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.241 line:92%
you talk about civic grace

00:00:08.241 --> 00:00:09.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you talk about
courageous empathy.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:12.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you speak a little bit
to what you mean by those idea

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.716 size:84% position:42%
and also the difficulty
in expressing those,

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.018 line:92%
in practicing those at a tim

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:21.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the opponent will
likely not be using those?

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:26.326
-Look, I was running on an Iow
stage, and we were so psyched.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.060 line:92%
Hundreds of people there.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.962 size:78% position:39%
I'm about to jump up,
and this guy sees me,

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:31.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
a former tight end
for Stanford University.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:31.965 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's a big guy.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:33.099 align:start size:94% position:6%
He puts his arm around me
and he goes,

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:36.202
"Dude, I want you to punch
Donald Trump in the face."

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I stop in my tracks
and I go,

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:40.440 line:92%
"Dude, that's a felony, man.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.310 size:81% position:41%
And, you know, this --
Donald Trump is a guy

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:48.982
who you understand he hurts you,
and my testosterone sometime

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:52.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
makes me want to
feel like punching him,

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:56.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
which would be bad for
this elderly, out-of-shape man

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:58.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he is if I did that.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.492 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:02.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
This physically --
physically weak specimen.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:03.296 line:92%
A physically weak specimen

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you see
what I'm talking there?

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:06.800 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's his tactics.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:11.237
And you don't beat a bully lik
him fighting him on his tactics,

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.806 line:92%
on his terms, using his turf

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:13.506 size:78% position:39% line:92%
He's the body shamer.

00:01:13.506 --> 00:01:17.143
He's the guy that shows -- tries
to drag people in the gutter

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I -- This is a moral momen
in America.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:23.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to me, what we need from
our next leader,

00:01:23.349 --> 00:01:26.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially after the time of
moral vandalism

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:27.120 size:88% position:44% line:92%
that we're in right now,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:30.023
is we need a leader that's not
gonna call us to the worst o

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
who we are but call us
to the best of who we are.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.360 line:92%
And we need to be, as a party --

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:39.165 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.866 size:78% position:39% line:92%
In this moral moment,

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
we need not to talk about
necessarily what we're against

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.470 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but what we're for,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the best way of looking at
this is just our history.

00:01:45.638 --> 00:01:48.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
The gardens of our democracy
have never been free of

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:52.378 size:81% position:41%
the weeds of bigotry,
hatred, a demagoguery.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.446 line:92%
Every generation has had them.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
I literally had an elder frien
of mine text me, saying,

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
listening to Donald Trump'
rally last week,

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:01.721 size:81% position:41%
that he was talking --
the words he was using

00:02:01.721 --> 00:02:03.990 align:start size:94% position:6%
reminded him of
a George Wallace rally

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he watched
in black and white

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:07.794 line:92%
and now it's in living color

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:09.462 line:92%
But how did we beat them before?

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:12.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all, don't mistak
strength for --

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be strong,
you need to be mean.

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
We beat Bull Connor,
for example, in Birmingham

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:20.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
not by bringing bigger dog
and bigger firehoses

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
and matching his demagoguery
with more.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
But these were incredible
artists of activism

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:28.014
that called to the moral
imagination of a country,

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:32.218
that called us to a greater --
a revival of that civic race

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:33.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
that pulled black folks
and white folks

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
and more folks together
that relegated that demagogu

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:38.458 line:92%
to the ash heap of history

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:42.328
We will not beat Donald Trum
by trying to be more like hi

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
but by showing
that we are not like him.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.266
We are not weak morally.
We are not weak mentally.

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're a strong nation,
and we're a nation that unites

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:52.071 size:84% position:42%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It does seem like --

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:55.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, it's going to b
a difficult undertaking

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.578
for whoever the nominee is
to take back the White House

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
It might even be
more statistically difficult

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.082 size:88% position:44%
for the Democratic Party
to take back the Senate.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:05.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, let's say
you're in the White House,

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Mitch McConnell
is still running the Senate.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.857
Where does -- Where can you find
any optimism to think

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:14.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you can get something don
as long as Mitch McConnell

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
who has been
incredibly effective,

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
no matter what
you think about him,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.500
effective in sort of havin
this Republican platform

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.269
that has been a wall that's been
impossible to break through.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, that's a distinction
of my record.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:28.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I was the mayor
of New Jersey's largest city

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.475 line:92%
in the middle of a recession

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:31.477 size:75% position:38%
where people told me
what we couldn't do,

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:33.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now from transforming
our school system

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:35.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the biggest period economic
development in 60 years,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:38.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
we got things done
people said couldn't be done

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:38.918 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I got to the Senate.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the things
that drove me there

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:41.721 line:92%
was the fact that we have

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:43.656 size:88% position:44%
one of the most shameful
criminal-justice systems

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.492
on the planet, where we sa
we're the land of the free

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:50.330
but we incarcerate 25% of
the globe's incarcerated people.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went there
to do something about it.

00:03:51.664 --> 00:03:53.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I remember people
in my own party telling me

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You're never gonna get
legislation like this passed

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:57.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
through the United States
Senate,

00:03:57.737 --> 00:04:00.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially freeing people
from prison at a time

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the aftermath of
Willie Horton,

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
where everybody
is gonna be afraid to do that.

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, with Mitch McConnell
there,

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:07.180 line:92%
I led from the Democratic side

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:11.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bill that not only got passe
but right now, last week,

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
we saw thousands of people
being released,

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:15.955
the overwhelming majority of
them being African-Americans

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:18.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is the First Step --
-The First Step Act.

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:21.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, so, I do not
resign myself ever

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:24.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
to people saying
things can't get done.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:27.867
And why I fight so hard
in this election, I tell people,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:31.170
I know that the number-one thing
people want in my party

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.005 line:92%
is just to beat Donald Trump

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:35.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I'm like, "That is a floor
It is not the ceiling.

00:04:35.441 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have to have
bigger aspirations."

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we make this election
all about him,

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.347 line:92%
that's a small man, one office

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:44.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not what I want
this election to just be about

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:45.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
We will beat him.
I will beat him.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.755
But we've got to make this
more of a movement electio

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
to create
new American majorities.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:53.192
And I'm not talking about
Democratic majorities.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:53.960 line:92%
But the fact of the matter

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.829 size:84% position:42%
is we actually agree on
more than we disagree.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:57.997 line:92%
The lines that divide us,

00:04:57.997 --> 00:05:00.033 size:81% position:41%
they're not as big as
the ties that bind us.

00:05:00.033 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I think our generation
now, and this election

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:07.774
and this moral moment has to
begin not to resign ourselve

00:05:07.774 --> 00:05:09.676 line:92%
to a fractured broken government

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:12.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
but aspire to do
what our ancestors did.

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.112 line:92%
We just came off a weekend

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:15.214 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they created
the new American majority

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
to defy the limits
of human potential

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:19.352 line:92%
and put a person on the moon

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:22.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's time for our generation
to begin to reject

00:05:22.588 --> 00:05:24.257 line:92%
divisive tribalistic politic

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
and inspire people
so that we in our generation

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:28.394 size:88% position:44% line:92%
can defy gravity as well

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.830
and do the things that other
people think are impossible.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Alright. Well, thanks for
making the time.

00:05:32.465 --> 00:05:34.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know it's got to be busy
out there.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:34.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Best of luck in the next roun
of debates.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:38.071 line:92%
That's Cory Booker, everybody.

